rp1-gpclk-dkms (1.1.1-1) UNRELEASED; urgency=medium

  * Recycle the ABI v2 candidate with route-specific, reboot-based,
    output-inhibited target-validation controls for GPIO4 and GPIO20.
  * Preserve the ABI v2 UAPI byte-for-byte and keep both routes unavailable
    until exact-build evidence is returned.
  * Install the versioned, route-neutral application route manager, JSON
    schema, and consumer contract without installing qualification controls.
  * Add disabled, group-restricted systemd socket activation so a running
    application can request a separately owned service-quiesce transaction.
  * Reject qualification archive generation for package bytes without an
    exact output-inhibited validation identity.
  * Preserve and report strictly validated completed historical journals and
    migrate the earlier package-owned route block only during a transaction.
  * Permit the fixed executor to create its same-directory atomic boot-file
    temporary while retaining a read-only system sandbox elsewhere.

